      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (William C. Ingram)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Likewise, we contend that brandish, based on the -- the text of the statute, the -- how legislatures have typically treated that fact and the fact that it involves a mens rea element -- that is, brandish is -- is defined as displaying or making the presence known of a firearm in order to intimidate and -- and mens rea has traditionally been an element -- and then based on the legislative history that those statutes would lead the Court to conclude, based on the statutory analysis, that brandish is in fact an element to be proved and not merely a sentencing enhancement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (William C. Ingram)",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- first of all, the -- the fact that the increase under the brandish statute goes from a mandatory minimum of 5 to a mandatory minimum of -- of 7 not being a steep increase, first of all, it does take the defendant 40 percent higher for brandishing from 5 to 7, and -- and it doubles the penalty 100 percent higher for discharging the firearm, which cannot be divorced from the brandishing element."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Can I -- can I go to Apprendi?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What you're saying is he has to be honest when he decides the brandishing issue."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Previously whatever you did under 924(c), the judge had no sentencing discretion at all. It was just 5 years or 20 years or 30 years. Congress changed that and said this is a more serious crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is precisely why we urge the Court to"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Dreeben, apart from one being within the jury zone and the other not, is there a rational distinction between saying, judge, you can't add on 2 years at the top and saying you can't subtract 2 years at the bottom?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is that the implication of Apprendi?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The States have a much wider range of mandatory minimum sentencing programs. They've filed an amicus brief in this case that itemizes the far greater number and wider range of State mandatory minimum programs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2001-00-10666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2dba323396db574abee852ed74d06579ba01a4084acf77cdae704daf7cd976da",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2dba323396db-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under 18 U.S.C., section 3553(e)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
